{%- comment -%}
  Announcement strip. Lives in the header group, above the header.

  The header group is pinned with `position: fixed` (layout/theme.liquid), so
  <main> carries a padding-top spacer equal to the group's height — 3.5rem /
  4rem, matching the header's h-14 / sm:h-16. Adding this bar makes the group
  taller, so the spacer has to grow by exactly the bar's height or the hero
  slides underneath.

  `bar_h` below is the single source of truth for that: it sets the bar's own
  height AND the corrected spacer, so the two can never drift apart. The <style>
  block only exists while the section is rendered, so removing or disabling the
  bar restores the original spacer with no leftover override.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign bar_h = 2.25
  assign bg = section.settings.bg_color | default: '#F6E7E4'
  assign fg = section.settings.text_color | default: '#895B3A'
-%}

{%- if section.settings.text != blank -%}
  <div
    data-announcement-bar
    class="flex w-full items-center justify-center px-4 text-center"
    style="height: {{ bar_h }}rem; background-color: {{ bg }}; color: {{ fg }};"
    {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    {%- if section.settings.link != blank -%}
      <a
        href="{{ section.settings.link }}"
        class="truncate text-xs tracking-[0.08em] underline-offset-4 transition hover:underline sm:text-sm"
      >{{ section.settings.text }}</a>
    {%- else -%}
      <p class="truncate text-xs tracking-[0.08em] sm:text-sm">{{ section.settings.text }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Shopify wraps EACH section of a group in its own div, and every one of them
    carries .shopify-section-group-header-group — which theme.liquid pins to
    `position: fixed; top: 0`. With one section that is fine; with two they stack
    at the same origin and the header paints straight over this bar. So offset
    every header-group wrapper that follows this one by the bar's height. The
    sibling combinator keeps it general: add a third header section later and it
    is offset too, with no extra rule.

    Then grow the <main> spacer to match. `#MainContent` is an id, so it outranks
    Tailwind's .pt-14 / .sm:pt-16 utilities without needing !important.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <style>
    .shopify-section-group-header-group[id$="__announcement"] ~ .shopify-section-group-header-group {
      top: {{ bar_h }}rem;
    }
    #MainContent { padding-top: calc(3.5rem + {{ bar_h }}rem); }
    @media (min-width: 640px) {
      #MainContent { padding-top: calc(4rem + {{ bar_h }}rem); }
    }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Announcement bar",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "text",
      "label": "Text",
      "default": "5% off on all products",
      "info": "Leave empty to hide the bar."
    },
    { "type": "url", "id": "link", "label": "Link (optional)" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "bg_color", "label": "Background", "default": "#F6E7E4" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "text_color", "label": "Text", "default": "#895B3A" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Announcement bar" }],
  "enabled_on": { "groups": ["header"] }
}
{% endschema %}
